metadata:
  name: Ossobuco alla milanese
  images:
    - https://i.imgur.io/W8bvyJT_d.webp?maxwidth=640&shape=thumb&fidelity=medium
  description: From https://www.greatitalianchefs.com/recipes/ossobuco-alla-milanese-recipe 
  types: [Main,Stew]

ingredients:
 - 4 u cross-cut veal shank, 3cm thick
 - 1 u flour, seasoned with salt and pepper
 - 1 u olive oil
 - 2 u onions, diced
 - 2 u celery sticks, diced
 - 1 u large carrot, diced
 - 1 u garlic clove, sliced
 - 1 u sprig of thyme
 - 1 u bay leaf
 - 2 tbsp of tomato purée
 - 500 ml white wine
 - 1 l chicken stock, hot
 - 10 g dried porcini mushrooms
 - 1 u salt
 - 1 u pepper

actions:
 - free_text To begin, place a heavy-based saucepan over a high heat and add a splash of oil. Dust the pieces of veal in seasoned flour and fry until nicely browned on both sides. Remove from the pan and set aside
 - free_text Turn the heat down and add another dash of oil with the onion, celery, carrot and garlic. Season with salt and sauté until softened
 - free_text Add the thyme, bay leaf and tomato purée and stir for a further 2 minutes
 - free_text Return the meat to the pan and pour in the wine. Reduce by a third then add the hot stock and dried mushrooms. Simmer for 2 hours, or until the meat is tender
